rota lap 4668, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes. Read the threshold, what-brix-infuse-is, the-happy-zone-and-the-thin-edge and growing-a-language. The row's instruction is literal here: taste what is in the box before cooking a second pot, and an infusion is tested by running it a SECOND time. This lap ran the second time.
think Reds first, and for once the red was mine and pointed at its own cure. The cold pass read 270 run, 266 green, 2 red -- stash_record on unlanded=1, and standing_equipment red_self on that. One root.
think The unlanded record is the session log my own previous lap wrote at 20260911.232518 and never committed. fleet_round_open.sh stashed the whole lap ten seconds before this one opened: 8 tracked files modified and 6 untracked, 737 lines, holding the paper, the shelf, the log, a scan, a control, a witness and a roster seat.
think Read the box before cooking: git stash show -p on the tracked half and git show on stash@{0}^3 for the untracked half. The work was finished -- the witness asserts 34 pen legs and six metal probes, and the paper reads Field with its own room named at the door.
think Recovered rather than rebuilt. git stash apply took it back with no conflict, since HEAD had not moved off the stash's base. Rebuilt glow/bin/glow_run from the recovered source, because the roster pass had built it from HEAD's and the probe half reads the binary.
obs The cold pass was the DEAD lap's own. It launched 20260911.230942, held construction/standing-equipment-run.lock.d through the kill, and --detach refused to open a second. The baton's own check is what named it: its header counts 22 stashes and lists stash@{0} as one from 20260910, where git stash list reads 23 and a stash from 20260911-233249. It closed honestly at tree_moved=no, because both its digests fell on a clean tree -- the dead lap's files were written after its open and stashed before its close.
obs So a roster pass outlives the lap that launched it. Nothing here is wrong: the lock held, the refusal was loud, the transcript was accurate. What a reader needs is the check the baton already prints, since the header's own stash list is what tells a live pass from an inherited one.
obs Landing the recovery closes both reds without touching either guard. stash_record reads landed=17 unlanded=0 verdict=ok with the files in the worktree alone -- the scan counts a worktree as a ref a reader reaches, which is why the gate closed before the commit rather than after it.
obs Second firing of this class on this pier inside three hours; the peer lap at 20260911.210824 recovered its own box the same way, and REDS %717 names a third that sat five days. The class is the round-open stash, and no round open reads it back.
obs First log of 20260912, so the day shelf, its row, and both roster rows are born in this commit -- session_roster_agree gates an uncounted shelf at zero. 20260911 keeps its open row: a day-close is the next day's duty and that reading passes free by name.
